        {
          "$type": "Models.Report, Models",
          "VariableNames": [
            "[Clock].Today",
            "",
            "([Soil].OutputNutrientLayers.NO3[1] + [Soil].OutputNutrientLayers.NH4[1]) as SoilN_0_15",
            "([Soil].OutputNutrientLayers.NO3[2] + [Soil].OutputNutrientLayers.NH4[2]) as SoilN_15_30",
            "([Soil].OutputNutrientLayers.NO3[3] + [Soil].OutputNutrientLayers.NH4[3]) as SoilN_30_60",
            "([Soil].OutputNutrientLayers.NO3[4] + [Soil].OutputNutrientLayers.NH4[4]) as SoilN_60_90",
            "([Soil].OutputNutrientLayers.NO3[5] + [Soil].OutputNutrientLayers.NH4[5]) as SoilN_90_120",
            "(SoilN_0_15 + SoilN_15_30 ) as SoilN_0_30",
            "(SoilN_0_15 + SoilN_15_30 + SoilN_30_60) as SoilN_0_60",
            "(SoilN_0_15 + SoilN_15_30 + SoilN_30_60 + SoilN_60_90) as SoilN_0_90",
            "(SoilN_0_90 + SoilN_90_120) as SoilN_0_120",
            "",
            "[Soil].Nutrient.MineralN",
            "[Soil].Nutrient.MineralisedN",
            "[Soil].OutputWaterLayers.SW",
            "",
            "",
            "[Soil].OutputWaterLayers.NO3[4] as LeachedN_70cm"
          ],
          "EventNames": [
            "",
            "[Clock].DoReport"
          ],
          "GroupByVariableName": null,
          "Name": "DailyReportWater_n_MineralN",
          "ResourceName": null,
          "Children": [
            {
              "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
              "Text": "Measurements \n\nSoil samples will be collected from each plot: \n\n0-15, 15-30 and 30-60 cm depths (or to stones). \n\nComposite sample of 10 cores 1 m apart following a 10 m transect across the plot. The intensive regime is to account for urine patch variability, and ensure we intercept a proportionally accurate number of urine patches across the plot. \n\nSoil mineral N (nitrate and ammonium) measured at every depth. \n\nBasic mineral analysis for 0-15 cm depth (combined sample from all reps). \n\nFollowing emergence, plant counts will be performed to assess achieved plant population \n\nCrop canopy development will be monitored at regular intervals using a hand-held Greenseeker (reflectance measurements). \n\nBiomass will be measured at three key crop stages of the ‘control treatment’ (all treatments simultaneously measured at each sampling occasion): \n\nGS21 (tillering), September \n\nGS32 (2nd node), October \n\nGS45 (booting) = final harvest, November \n\n \n\nFor each biomass harvest, 3x 0.5 m2 quadrats (1.5 m2 in total) in each plot will be cut at ground level and total fresh biomass weighed. A ≈300g subsample will be taken, weighed after drying at 60°C until constant weight (dry matter content), and then ground and analysed for total N content using a LECO CNS analyser in order to determine crop N uptake. \n\n \n\nAt final harvest, a separate subsample will also be taken and sent to Hills Laboratories to measure feed quality. \n\n \n\nClimate data (rainfall, air and soil temperature, radiation) will be recorded via a local NIWA or on-site weather station for each site. \n\n ",
              "Name": "Memo",
              "ResourceName": null,
              "Children": [],
              "Enabled": true,
              "ReadOnly": false
            }
          ],
          "Enabled": true,
          "ReadOnly": false
        },
